# An unapproved build script must not be able to fail a deployment.
#
# pnpm 10 refuses to run a dependency's postinstall unless the package is named
# in onlyBuiltDependencies, and by default it treats anything ignored as a fatal
# ERR_PNPM_IGNORED_BUILDS. esbuild is approved below and in pnpm-workspace.yaml,
# so in the normal case nothing is ignored and this setting never comes up.
#
# It is here for the case where that approval is not honoured — a different pnpm
# version on the build runner reading a different config location, a transitive
# dependency that adds a build script tomorrow. Then the install warns and
# carries on instead of killing the deploy.
#
# That is safe rather than a paper-over, and the reason is specific: the only
# packages with build scripts here are three copies of esbuild, pulled in by tsx,
# vitest and drizzle-kit. All three are dev tooling for tests and scripts.
# `next build` does not use esbuild, and has been verified to succeed with its
# postinstall skipped entirely. A production build cannot be broken by this.
#
# (An earlier version of this file set strict-dep-builds=true, to make local
# installs fail the way CI does. That was the wrong trade for a deploy: it turns
# a survivable warning into a dead build.)
strict-dep-builds=false
